From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: Report the option lock to the OS in a
 volatile variable

The arm of coreboot's option lock (SMMSTORE_CMD_OPTION_LOCK, edk2/0056)
left no trace the OS could read: coreboot's SMM console is compiled out
without DEBUG_SMI, as in release builds, and the payload's DEBUG lines are
not in a release build either. PlatformLockFirmwareSlots() now writes the
EFI_STATUS that SmmStoreLibOptionLock() returned, as a UINT64, to the
volatile variable OptionLockStatus of the coreboot options GUID
(BS+RT): EFI_SUCCESS armed, EFI_UNSUPPORTED with no option lock or
BIOS Lock off. It is the payload's report of the answer of SMM, not a
reading of the state there.

So that the OS can read it and not fake it, PlatformBootManagerBeforeConsole()
registers a lock-on-create Variable Policy for the name before EndOfDxe,
which closes Variable Policy to new rules: the first write, at
ReadyToBoot, goes in, any write after it is refused, and a non-volatile
variable of that name cannot be created.
---
diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
index 5250259..c11786e 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
@@ -1,891 +1,897 @@
